<p>
"Clutter" is one block code (<code>clutter</code>, plus the <code>clutter-devastation</code> and
<code>clutter-aquatic</code> variants) with the <code>ShapeFromAttributes</code> behavior: what it
actually <em>is</em> &mdash; a skull, a statue, a barricade, a broken anvil &mdash; is a per-instance
<code>type</code> attribute on the placed block, not part of its code. That is why the item index
only ever shows a bare "Clutter" entry.
</p>
<p>
Like tapestries, every worldgen schematic a structure actually references is pre-filtered (from its
header block-code list) down to those containing a clutter code, then fully decoded: each
<code>BlockEntities</code> value is Ascii85-decoded into a <code>TreeAttribute</code> whose
<code>type</code> string (e.g. <code>skull/human-crystal</code>) is read. Types are then grouped, with
which structures place each and how many times.
</p>
<p>
Names come from the game's own lang keys, built the way <code>BlockClutter</code> builds them:
<code>clutter-</code> + the type with <code>/</code> replaced by <code>-</code>. A type with no such
key is shown by its raw type string and flagged.
</p>
<div class="coverage-note">
<p><strong>Schematic-authored, not guaranteed.</strong> This is what the structure schematics
contain; some clutter is also scattered by <code>stackrandomizer-clutter</code>/loot mechanisms at
world generation, which isn't visible in schematic data.</p>
</div>
<div class="coverage-note">
<p><strong>Decoder.</strong> The <code>TreeAttribute</code> layouts follow the game's own
<code>vsapi</code> source (<code>libs/vs-schematic/src/schematicDecode.ts</code>). Every block entity in the
vanilla and BetterRuins schematics decodes without error (<code>npm run decode-stats</code>), and
<code>npm test</code> pins each attribute type.</p>
</div>

<h3>Detail pages and 3D models</h3>
<p>
Each type has its own page with a rotatable, untextured 3D model. The shape comes from the blocktype's
<code>attributes.types</code> entry whose <code>code</code> equals the type, mirroring the game's
<code>BlockShapeFromAttributes.LoadTypes</code>: <code>&lt;shapeBasePath&gt;/&lt;code&gt;.json</code> unless the entry has its own
<code>shapePath</code> (relative to the same folder, or absolute under <code>shapes/</code> when it starts with
<code>/</code>). A few types (<code>carcass-fish</code>, some Maltie's Firearms piles and wall mounts) name no shape that exists, so they have no model.
Placement variation the game applies per block (random rotation and height jitter) is not shown.
</p>
